{"actor":{"harness":"claude-code","run_id":"signoff-a-20261028-16f7","station":"signoff-v2"},"at":"2026-10-28T00:00:00Z","claim":"the hyphen rule reaches only the events, so result.json and chat.md (`result.py:128` and `:137`) still show the separator form while the log and verdict doc show the hyphen form, and nothing in chat says the two differ.","finding":"f1:bf87234d01000b514479","kind":"finding_raised","ledger_doc":"docs/plans/2026-10-28-e18-fix-round-2.md","location":{"file":"plugins/signoff-v2/skills/signoff-v2/scripts/signoff_core/records_write.py","line":224,"line_end":null,"more":[],"raw":"plugins/signoff-v2/skills/signoff-v2/scripts/signoff_core/records_write.py:224","resolved":true,"tag":null},"origin":{"kind":"native"},"prev":"73170db03b794376c2d8acbc9c967a93407c1d3a540103428ba3c439c50e9190","raised_by":"A","scenario":"a reviewer quotes a /fb line in a claim, the run records, the chat block prints the claim with the separator while the verdict doc and build-doc block print the hyphen form, and a reader comparing chat to the record sees two different texts. The spec names only the log, the verdict doc and the punch list, so this is low confidence.","seq":7,"severity":"MINOR","slice":"A","source":{"identity":{"commit":"e35469e8e4f9dc3fd89214ae75ff73c246c01db1","dirty":false,"submodules":[],"tracked_diff_sha256":"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855","untracked":[],"untracked_sha256":"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855"},"known":true},"v":1}
{"actor":{"harness":"claude-code","run_id":"signoff-a-20261028-16f7","station":"signoff-v2"},"at":"2026-10-28T00:00:00Z","claim":"`unseparated` only rewrites a full space-dot-space inside a field. A claim that starts with \"dot space\" or ends with \"space dot\" records cleanly, but once it is rendered as `(<claim>)` between two separators it gives a build-doc line that the station's own Appendix A strict check later refuses. The doc then blocks every later run.","finding":"f1:1d0f1870687bfea6088f","kind":"finding_raised","ledger_doc":"docs/plans/2026-10-28-e18-fix-round-2.md","location":{"file":"plugins/signoff-v2/skills/signoff-v2/scripts/signoff_core/records_write.py","line":193,"line_end":null,"more":[],"raw":"plugins/signoff-v2/skills/signoff-v2/scripts/signoff_core/records_write.py:193","resolved":true,"tag":null},"origin":{"kind":"native"},"prev":"a6246586ca4ea6ac51bcd17818634506748aba657582a49f3eea9e0d270c9208","raised_by":"A","scenario":"the answer's finding claim is \"pad() is short by one\" followed by a space and a middle dot (or starts with a middle dot and a space). record-answer exits 0 and record ends completed (exit 10). A fresh check-input plus scope on the same build doc then stops missing_input / legacy_ambiguous on the line `- MAJOR - src/signpost/pad.py:6 - (pad() is short by one <dot>) - ...`, so no later signoff or recheck can level that doc. The scenario field does not have this problem because the component's render turns a trailing dot into a hyphen. Base 199fb0a behaves the same way, so this is a gap the hyphen rule leaves open, not a regression.","seq":8,"severity":"MINOR","slice":"A","source":{"identity":{"commit":"e35469e8e4f9dc3fd89214ae75ff73c246c01db1","dirty":false,"submodules":[],"tracked_diff_sha256":"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855","untracked":[],"untracked_sha256":"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855"},"known":true},"v":1}
{"actor":{"harness":"claude-code","run_id":"signoff-a-20261028-16f7","station":"signoff-v2"},"at":"2026-10-28T00:00:00Z","claim":"the separator rule covers the claim, scenario and location of raised findings only. The verdict doc's method lines (signoff.py:1416-1437) copy each check's name, command and output head, and the reviewer's session id and model, unchanged, so those fields can still put the separator into the verdict doc.","finding":"f1:f98abcb210a0ed5ed1d6","kind":"finding_raised","ledger_doc":"docs/plans/2026-10-28-e18-fix-round-2.md","location":{"file":"plugins/signoff-v2/skills/signoff-v2/scripts/signoff_core/records_write.py","line":224,"line_end":null,"more":[],"raw":"plugins/signoff-v2/skills/signoff-v2/scripts/signoff_core/records_write.py:224","resolved":true,"tag":null},"origin":{"kind":"native"},"prev":"691b1d0a237b749ed09de0761414d6c702f1d79f0012d0e2f9d80c02f4501fd1","raised_by":"A","scenario":"a reviewer's checks_executed row has the output \"- 2026-10-28 <dot> GUIDE <dot> ...\" (a /fb line printed by a grep). The verdict doc holds the raw separator outside any finding, and the SEPARATOR_NOTE is not written because quotes_separator looks only at raised findings. I found nothing that parses those lines today (level runs only on the build doc), so the harm is limited to the doc's statement being incomplete.","seq":9,"severity":"MINOR","slice":"A","source":{"identity":{"commit":"e35469e8e4f9dc3fd89214ae75ff73c246c01db1","dirty":false,"submodules":[],"tracked_diff_sha256":"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855","untracked":[],"untracked_sha256":"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855"},"known":true},"v":1}
{"actor":{"harness":"claude-code","run_id":"signoff-a-20261028-16f7","station":"signoff-v2"},"at":"2026-10-28T00:00:00Z","claim":"The new `unseparated` duplicates a scrub rule that already exists, and the two disagree. `record_grammar._single_line` (record_grammar.py:519-522) already writes `SEP` as \" - \" and also writes any bare \"·\" as \"-\" and any line break as a space. The new helper handles only the spaced form, so the station now has two rules for one reserved character.","finding":"f1:7d450a29784059315c27","kind":"finding_raised","ledger_doc":"docs/plans/2026-10-28-e18-fix-round-2.md","location":{"file":"plugins/signoff-v2/skills/signoff-v2/scripts/signoff_core/records_write.py","line":185,"line_end":null,"more":[],"raw":"plugins/signoff-v2/skills/signoff-v2/scripts/signoff_core/records_write.py:185","resolved":true,"tag":null},"origin":{"kind":"native"},"prev":"fb374fcdac1d295af0daa52030ae88e2bacb4b673bb8a845303350f7b02dbf4d","raised_by":"A","scenario":"A finding claim \"see a·b\" is recorded unchanged by the native path, while the pilot's renderer would write \"see a-b\". The log, the build doc and a v1-rendered line then hold different text for the same reviewer words.","seq":10,"severity":"MINOR","slice":"A","source":{"identity":{"commit":"e35469e8e4f9dc3fd89214ae75ff73c246c01db1","dirty":false,"submodules":[],"tracked_diff_sha256":"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855","untracked":[],"untracked_sha256":"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855"},"known":true},"v":1}
{"actor":{"harness":"claude-code","run_id":"signoff-a-20261028-16f7","station":"signoff-v2"},"at":"2026-10-28T00:00:00Z","claim":"A claim with a line break still passes `record-answer` and is refused only late, at `record`. That is the same late-failure class as defect 1. The answer schema puts no constraint on claim, scenario or location, and nothing in the slice scrubs `\\r` or `\\n`. The plan's \"No other change\" may put this deliberately out of scope.","finding":"f1:1e7c249402e4fc54c601","kind":"finding_raised","ledger_doc":"docs/plans/2026-10-28-e18-fix-round-2.md","location":{"file":"plugins/signoff-v2/skills/signoff-v2/scripts/signoff_core/records_write.py","line":193,"line_end":null,"more":[],"raw":"plugins/signoff-v2/skills/signoff-v2/scripts/signoff_core/records_write.py:193","resolved":true,"tag":null},"origin":{"kind":"native"},"prev":"13f42f6727f8c6f8b49ac39829cf3aa126fffc6165e84ba05bddea11f12577e4","raised_by":"A","scenario":"The reviewer answers with claim \"line one\\nline two\". `record-answer` exits 0. At `record`, the records event schema refuses the claim under pattern `[\\r\\n]` (my probe confirmed the refusal), so the run stops `recording_failed` after the review has finished.","seq":11,"severity":"MINOR","slice":"A","source":{"identity":{"commit":"e35469e8e4f9dc3fd89214ae75ff73c246c01db1","dirty":false,"submodules":[],"tracked_diff_sha256":"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855","untracked":[],"untracked_sha256":"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855"},"known":true},"v":1}
{"actor":{"harness":"claude-code","run_id":"signoff-a-20261028-16f7","station":"signoff-v2"},"at":"2026-10-28T00:00:00Z","claim":"The verdict doc's note and the scrub catch only the exact form (a space, a middle dot, a space), so a middle dot at the edge of a field with no space on one side passes the schema unchanged, and the renderer's own separator join can turn it into a separator.","finding":"f1:d19ae1071f19e7a0d02c","kind":"finding_raised","ledger_doc":"docs/plans/2026-10-28-e18-fix-round-2.md","location":{"file":"plugins/signoff-v2/skills/signoff-v2/scripts/signoff_core/records_write.py","line":203,"line_end":null,"more":[],"raw":"plugins/signoff-v2/skills/signoff-v2/scripts/signoff_core/records_write.py:203","resolved":true,"tag":null},"origin":{"kind":"native"},"prev":"d9689d433cdd85c4f2a872a3235746021d1192ddf0a957282a9f7ca1b485ed89","raised_by":"A","scenario":"A scenario that ends \"GUIDE\" plus a space and a middle dot is recorded unchanged; in the build doc it renders as \"GUIDE\", then a space and a middle dot, then the join's own space, middle dot and space, then \"A\"; the component's native-line recognition should set that line aside, so the next run's level dry run should not stop, but I did not run this.","seq":12,"severity":"MINOR","slice":"A","source":{"identity":{"commit":"e35469e8e4f9dc3fd89214ae75ff73c246c01db1","dirty":false,"submodules":[],"tracked_diff_sha256":"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855","untracked":[],"untracked_sha256":"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855"},"known":true},"v":1}
